                <pb facs="0451" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1231/88: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-26T18:00:00-05:00">January 26, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Your No. 3, January 25, 5 p.m. Studies relating to agreement with Mexico have
                    been going on here for some time and are nearing completion. I hope to be able
                    to inform you shortly when this Government will be able to proceed with the
                    discussions with the representatives of Mexico. If agreeable to the Mexican
                    authorities it is desired that the discussions take place in Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
